From 1bfb51770bff19051a0c74deeda080a14a201a6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James <spadent@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:33:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] No fast disk access while the program is making sound

A spinning Disk II ran the machine at up to 100 times its speed, even when
a game left the motor on while it played. As AppleWin does, fast disk
access now waits until the speaker has been quiet for 0.2 s and the
Mockingboard for 0.1 s of Apple time, and a burst stops as soon as sound
starts. Keypad + / - / * and Scroll Lock now say on screen that they
changed the speed. The PR#n hard disk test waits for DOS to finish loading
before it types, which the boot beep (now run at 1x) had exposed.
